{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122925-so-double-militance-or-how-to-drop-a-covenant","id":1122925,"title":"So double militance or how to drop a covenant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-30T23:40:44-07:00","id":1122925,"title":"So double militance or how to drop a covenant?","content":"two questions:<br /> Is it possible to be part of two covenants ? like on one city be a carthian while in another turf be a ordo dracul?<br /> second: lets say your PC gets expelled, what would be the process to join another covenant? would be the same process if he felt like &quot;i dont fit&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T00:03:59-07:00","id":1122930,"title":"","content":"There are merits in Secrets of the Covenants that allow you to have the benefit of low status (1 point) in a covenant without officially being a member. So you could be a full member of one covenant while having the appropriate merit for a second. The merits each cost 2 points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T00:04:46-07:00","id":1122931,"title":"","content":"From the 2e core alone, a character can join up to 4 covenants, p. 113. This should still make sense. If covenants are at war then a covenant probably won't want someone affiliated with their enemy. Covenants are usually eager to accept new members, so unless a covenant knows a character was expelled, the reason for expulsion, and would likewise expel someone under the same circumstances, I don't think a covenant cares if a character isn't liked elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T04:08:36-07:00","id":1122963,"title":"","content":"It depends on the setting. Most covenants allow cross membership, they just don't allow those members to reach the highest levels of leadership. Some people here will tell you you can't be both Sanctified and Acolyte or Carthian and Invictus but that's not true. It could be a Carthian regime retaining control with the help of Invictus stamping out any religious practices so they unite to preserve their beliefs and survive a communist style religious purge. The Invictus and Carthians may get sick of cleaning up the Masquerade breaches of Acolyte child sacrifices or Theban grave robbing and corpse defilement. Or all four of them could unite against a Dragon rule where non-Dragons can be abducted and experimented upon at any time by any Dragon. <br /> As to whether or not you can up and leave, that also depends on the setting. It may be as simple as simply not showing up and participating in covenant activities. Maybe it requires a formal resignation or departure ceremony. Maybe the only way out is by final death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T13:40:13-07:00","id":1123995,"title":"","content":"This thread reminds of that episode of <i>Seinfeld</i> where George tries to manipulate his girlfriend into agreeing to break up with him by dating somebody else and &quot;accidentally&quot; mixing up dates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:40:23-07:00","id":1124042,"title":"","content":"There was a Carthian merit that allowed you to take status on another covenant as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:13:36-07:00","id":1124060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122925-so-double-militance-or-how-to-drop-a-covenant?p=1124042#post1124042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a Carthian merit that allowed you to take status on another covenant as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right to Return makes it so your Carthian Status doesn't count towards the cap for Covenant status, but you lose the 10-again quality for any rolls to hide suspicious activity from your covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T07:53:11-07:00","id":1124299,"title":"","content":"Also Thousand Years of Night allows elders to have stuff from covenants they're not part of with the justification that they hopped ship at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T06:29:16-07:00","id":1125194,"title":"","content":"I rather see this from a narrative standpoint rather than a mechanical one. If a character is an Invictus spy infiltrating the Carthians I can see her having both Invictus and Carthian status. The plot control the rules not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T06:34:58-07:00","id":1125196,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the precariousness of the merit (you lose one if anyone finds out about the other) is enough of a drawback to let it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T09:21:04-07:00","id":1125253,"title":"","content":"As others have said, there are plenty of rules that support multiple Covenant membership, if that's the path you want the character to take. There is a cap to Covenant Status in such a case, but you can subscribe to up to four different Covenants by it. A Merit (Right of Return) allows to ignore Carthian Status for the purpose of the cap. Another one (Twilight Judge) can effectively make yourself or anyone you support above Ordo Dracul law, including the rules on membership, learning Mysteries, or forbidden lore. Yet other Merits (Casual User, Chorister, One Foot in the Door, Laity, Independent Study) allow to have the benefits of low status in a Covenant w/o being an official member. And elders can have stuff from covenants even if they aren't members, under the assumption they once joined for a while, then left. The combination of these rules indicates Kindred society does not care that much about cross membership (although it causes some suspicion) as long as the character does not try to claim leadership within multiple Covenants, betrays one organization for another, or spreads house secrets to non-members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 08-05-2017, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}